FORTRESS SHIELD — ACTIVE DOME
Still source image for frame 1 of idle animation 1

REFERENCE IMAGE INPUT

Attach `assets_src/loadout/spell-cards/loadout_spell_fortress_shield_card.png`
as the visual reference. Treat it as the source of truth for the shield's
blue-cyan and restrained gold energy palette, luminous reflections, and
painterly fantasy-game finish. Do not copy its fortress, landscape, sky,
trees, composition, or card-art framing. Generate one isolated battlefield
effect sprite.

PROMPT

Create exactly one still 2D game sprite: the pristine, fully active Fortress
Shield energy dome, intended to be the first frame of a subtle idle animation.
Show one complete, closed, translucent oval barrier in a fixed orthographic
side view matching a 2D siege battlefield. Its centered oval silhouette must
read as a protective dome wrapped around an invisible fortress footprint,
not as a flat ring, a half-arch, or a top-only canopy. Keep its overall shape
symmetrical and close to a 4:3 width-to-height ratio, matching the game's
fortress-centered shield geometry.

Render only the magical barrier. The fortress, catapult, ground, projectiles,
and battlefield are absent; the asset will be composited over the live
fortress in-game. Keep the oval's interior transparent so the fortress
remains clearly visible underneath. Give the barrier a very light,
translucent blue-cyan membrane with a crisp but delicate luminous edge,
subtle painterly refraction, a few soft flowing magical reflections, and
sparse tiny glints along the shell. Add restrained warm-gold highlights as
reflections within the blue-cyan energy, not as a second outline. Keep the
effect elegant and readable at small battlefield scale; avoid a busy pattern
or a solid opaque fill.

This is a quiet, undamaged full-health idle state. The energy is already
active and gently shimmering, but caught at one calm instant: no impact
flash, expanding pulse, cracks, holes, fading, or damage marks. Do not bake
health-dependent fading into the image; the game will make the dome more
transparent as the shield loses health. Keep the effect neutral and
team-agnostic, with no faction emblems or directional asymmetry.

TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS

- Output exactly one PNG at 1024 x 768 pixels, RGBA with genuine alpha
  transparency.
- Use a transparent background, not a checkerboard or a dark/colored matte.
- Center the complete dome precisely on the canvas and keep its silhouette
  and glow fully inside the image with a modest transparent safety margin.
- Preserve clean, soft alpha edges without a black, white, or colored fringe.
- Keep the oval shell proportion consistent with a 4:3 fortress footprint.
- No animation, sprite sheet, alternate takes, contact sheet, or variations.

